<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01P6">Remark <span data-tag="01P6">4.6.1.20</span>.</a> Let $q: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets, let $X$ and $Y$ be vertices of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let $e: q(X) \rightarrow q(Y)$ be an edge of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. Form a pullback diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}' \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [d]^{q} \\ \Delta ^1 \ar [r]^-{e} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, } \]
</div>
<p> so that $X$ lifts uniquely to a vertex $\widetilde{X} \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$ lying over the vertex $0 \in \Delta ^1$, and $Y$ lifts uniquely to a vertex $\widetilde{Y} \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$ lying over the vertex $1 \in \Delta ^1$. Remark <a data-tag="01P5" href="/tag/01P5">4.6.1.19</a> and Example <a data-tag="01P3" href="/tag/01P3">4.6.1.17</a> supply isomorphisms </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,Y)_{e} \simeq \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'}( \widetilde{X}, \widetilde{Y} )_{ \operatorname{id}_{\Delta ^1} } = \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'}( \widetilde{X}, \widetilde{Y} ). \]
</div>
</article>
